            <div xml:id="d617">

                <pb facs="0681" n="577" xml:id="pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002 Manchuria/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-12T12:00:00+00:00">March 12,
                        1932—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 12—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>107. Foreign Office informed me this morning it had received information
                    corresponding with paragraph 1 of Department’s 88, March 11, 1 p.m. Foreign
                    Office intimated its realization that some action along the lines of the
                    Department’s suggestion must be taken but could give no considered opinion
                    before consultation with Sir John Simon who returns from the Continent tomorrow
                    evening.</p>
                <p>I understand Minister Wilson was unable to communicate the contents of
                    Department’s 88, March 11, 1 p.m., to Simon before he left Geneva for Paris last
                    evening.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
